      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The central debate over economic sanctions involves a tension between their stated humanitarian goals and their often real-world outcomes. Proponents argue they are a necessary coercive tool to influence state behavior toward international norms like democracy and human rights. Critics, however, point out that sanctions frequently harm ordinary citizens more than they change elite decision-making, often serving as a projection of great power influence. Therefore, their effectiveness depends heavily on the design of the sanctions and the political context in which they are applied.",
