      "content": "Your critique touches upon the significant ethical tension in modern foreign policy regarding sanctions. If the humanitarian cost consistently outweighs the political gain, employing them under the banner of human rights can indeed appear hypocritical. Critics argue this turns the \"human rights\" justification into a convenient pretext for geopolitical maneuvering or maintaining regional dominance. Therefore, moving beyond the rhetoric suggests that a genuine commitment to human rights would likely demand alternative, less destructive forms of international pressure.",
